# E338 draft - OHOS native Autotools toolchain and config.status TMPDIR closure

id:                     E528
trigger_tool:           configure|config.status|libtool|make
phase:                  configuration|compilation|packaging
error_signature:        could not determine .* interface|configure: error: could not setup config files machinery|conf.*/subs1.awk: Permission denied|checking for .*ar.*link -lib|cannot create .*subs1.awk

severity:               3
category:               ohos, autotools, conan, permissions, native-toolchain
match_keywords:         libunwind, Autotools, config.status, llvm-ar, llvm-ranlib, mktemp, TMPDIR, replace_in_file, HMDFS, /data/storage/el2/base, /data/service/hnp/bin, shadow CI
title:                  Close the OHOS native Autotools environment before configure

root_cause:             On OHOS shadow CI, the runner profile can provide clang through tools.build:compiler_executables while PATH still omits the full native toolchain directory. Autotools then fails archiver discovery and may fall through to unrelated host tools such as link -lib. After that is fixed, Autoconf config.status can create ./conf* subdirectories under the build folder with ownership/permission semantics that reject creating generated files such as subs1.awk.
affected_scope:         Dependency-light Autotools release-tarball recipes that run configure natively on OHOS and rely on Conan profile compiler paths instead of a globally complete PATH.
verification_cmd:       CI_PACKAGES="archives/l/libunwind/1.6.2" zsh ci/conan/build_and_test.sh

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           recipe-local-ohos-autotools-env-closure
rec_description:        In generate(), derive the tool directory from tools.build:compiler_executables['c']; prepend it to PATH; define AR, NM, RANLIB, and STRIP to llvm-* tools when present. For OHOS, create a device-private TMPDIR such as /data/storage/el2/base/<pkg>-configure-tmp and use replace_in_file(strict=True) after apply_conandata_patches() to make the generated configure/config.status template create conf* below TMPDIR instead of the build folder.
rec_command:            conan create archives/l/libunwind/1.6.2 --build=missing
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-recipe

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      explicit-configure-shell-and-make-j1
fallback_description:   If the host shell or make jobserver adds noise, invoke configure through sh from build_folder and keep make at -j1. This does not replace the toolchain and mktemp closure; it only reduces unrelated OHOS runner variability.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          conan-recipe

forbid_1_pattern:       patch.*ci/conan|edit.*ohos-test-runner|export PATH=.*profile-wide
forbid_1_reason:        A package PR must not fix a package-local Autotools environment by modifying shared CI or runner infrastructure.
forbid_1_consequence:   The recipe remains non-reproducible outside that one runner and violates one-library-one-PR isolation.
forbid_2_pattern:       chmod.*conf.*|retry.*configure|ignore.*Permission denied
forbid_2_reason:        The config.status failure is deterministic HMDFS temporary-directory behavior, not a flaky chmod issue.
forbid_2_consequence:   Retries keep failing or advance only when unrelated environment state changes.

principles:             P013,P014
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             E114,E337
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

